# Transcript quotes

A direct quote from a transcript is the speaker’s words, not a label, status, or summary.

Whenever a direct quote is shown:

- Wrap it in quotation marks: “quote”
- Italicize it
- Do not add a second pair of marks if the stored text already has them
- Leave non-quotes in roman type with no marks. That includes behavior names, turn labels, “No quote stored,” and generated summaries

```html
<p class="transcript-quote">“Then there’s the risk that we simply don’t get the degree of symptom relief you’re hoping for.”</p>
```

```css
.transcript-quote { font-style: italic; }
```
